# Backend Docker build-context exclusions.
#
# backend/Dockerfile copies the whole context with `COPY . /app/backend/`, and
# Docker does not read .gitignore. Without this file a local `docker build`
# bakes backend/.env — the live Supabase service-role key, the Upstash password,
# the Qdrant API key, the JWT/encryption secrets and every provider key — into
# an image layer, and copies the entire .venv on top of it. CI and Render build
# from a clean checkout, but the documented "build from source" path and
# release.yml's `docker buildx` run against a working tree that does have
# backend/.env, so this exclusion is load-bearing. Mirrors frontend/.dockerignore.

# Secrets and local runtime state — never ship these.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.dev_secrets.json
*.db
mem0_history.db

# Virtualenv: the image installs its own dependencies into site-packages.
.venv
venv
__pycache__
*.py[cod]

# Tooling and test caches / artifacts
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.bandit
htmlcov
.coverage
coverage.xml
*.log

# Not needed at runtime
tests

# VCS and editor noise
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.idea

# Docker's own files (avoids a redundant context scan)
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
